ikli","dish/tsvikli"],["Tzimmes","dish/tzimmes"],["Wolfie Cohen's Rascal House","dish/wolfie-cohen-s-rascal-house"]]}]},"dish/patatas-bravas":{"t":"dish","r":"dish/patatas-bravas","n":"Patatas bravas","c":"#ede6da","crumb":[["Dishes","dishes"]],"sub":"Dish from Spanish cuisine","dot":"#cf5f87","intro":[["Patatas bravas is a dish native to Spain. It typically consists of white potatoes that have been cut into two-centimeter-wide (3⁄4-inch) cubes, then fried in oil and served hot with a spicy \"brava\" sauce. The brava sauce is primarily sweet or smoked paprika (using high-quality Spanish pimentón de la Vera and olive-oil-based, often thickened with cornstarch. Some regions call for the addition of tomato paste, although there can be many variations."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"dish-patatas-bravas"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Patatas_bravas"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's from","links":[["Spanish cuisine","cuisine/spanish-cuisine"]]},{"h":"Ingredients","count":1,"links":[["Potato","ingredient/potato"]]},{"h":"Cook it","rows":[{"name":"Spain on a Fork","ref":"site/spainonafork-com","color":"#55b8ad","shape":"site","sub":"spainonafork.com","note":"Albert Bevia's video channel and site of traditional and everyday Spanish recipes.","url":"https://spainonafork.com/welcome2/","suggested":true}]},{"h":"More from Spanish cuisine","links":[["Andrajos","dish/andrajos"],["Ataula","dish/ataula"],["Bolinhos de bacalhau","dish/bolinhos-de-bacalhau"],["Buñuelo","dish/bunuelo"],["Caldo galego","dish/caldo-galego"],["Chistorra","dish/chistorra"],["Churro","dish/churro"],["Cocido","dish/cocido"],["Cuajada","dish/cuajada"],["El Quijote (restaurant)","dish/el-quijote-restaurant"],["El Willy","dish/el-willy"],["Embutido","dish/embutido"],["Esquina Común","dish/esquina-comun"],["Gazpacho","dish/gazpacho"],["Hojuela","dish/hojuela"],["Jamón","dish/jamon"],["Migas","dish/migas"],["Mojo (sauce)","dish/mojo-sauce"],["Ogasawara-Hakushaku-Tei"